<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fangataufa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fangataufa is an uninhabited atoll in the Tuamotu archipelago of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moruroa">Moruroa</a>. With Moruroa, it was the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s Pacific nuclear tests from 1966 to 1996; it hosted the first French thermonuclear test, Canopus, in August 1968, and later underground tests. The atoll remains a restricted military zone.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fangataufa.jpg" alt="Fangataufa" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA Johnson Space Center - Earth Sciences and Image Analysis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fangataufa.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
